1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Official letters carry your name, address and account number.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Pasting one into a cloud chatbot hands all of that over.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Firebase AI Logic can run Gemini on your device. But in PREFER_ON_DEVICE mode, if this browser has no model, the SDK sends the raw letter to the cloud: 9 of 9 details.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Plain Letter never does. The cloud only ever gets a masked copy you approved: 0 of 9.

5
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:46,000
In Chrome with Gemini Nano, the letter is read on this device.

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Reading on device. Chrome's network log (bottom right) stays at 0 requests.

7
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:05,000
The answer, in Spanish: what it is, what to do, by when, what if you do nothing. Nothing was sent.

8
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:13,000
A six-page letter is too long for the on-device model.

9
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:20,000
So Plain Letter hides personal details first, on the device.

10
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:38,000
You see exactly what would be sent. Names, address, case number, date of birth: replaced. Deadlines and amounts stay.

11
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Only after you press Send does anything leave. Gemini in the cloud answers; your details are put back on your device.

12
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:08,000
The ledger shows the exact request body. One request in Chrome's log. Our tests check that the two are identical and contain none of your details.

13
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Tested: masking, the ledger, the naive mode. Measured on real Gemini Nano: 23.5 of 24 answer fields right, every name found.

14
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Plain Letter. Understand a letter without handing it over.

